    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d645">

                <pb facs="0799" n="725" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg725"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 871.51/57a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-01T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 1, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1674. Department is uneasy regarding the Roumanian situation and desires to avail
                    itself of Colonel Judson’s<anchor n="1" xml:id="d645-f1"/>
                    experience and <pb facs="0800" n="726" xml:id="pg726"/> knowledge of this
                    situation. The War Department therefore instructs him to proceed to Jassy to
                    obtain the information requested in the Department’s 1675 September 1, 6
                    p.m.</p>
                <p>As soon as possible after his arrival in Jassy the Department desires a cable
                    report from him as to whether in his opinion there is any danger of Roumania
                    making terms with the enemy governments, and if so what will be the most
                    practical means of keeping Roumania with the Allies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d645-f1" n="1" xml:id="d645-f1-content">
                <p>Brig. Gen. W. V. Judson, military attaché at Petrograd.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
